      "observed": "Two ATtiny microcontrollers (U2: ATtiny13V-10S and U4: ATtiny45-20P) are connected pin-to-pin on all I/O, reset, and power nets.",
      "expected": "Only one ATtiny should be populated; the other should be removed or marked DNP.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"6\") (name \"NET0001\") (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\")) (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"6\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "If both are populated, they will contend on shared nets, causing programming failure, I/O contention, and possible damage.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies: U2 has an incompatible SOIC-8W footprint for an ATtiny13V-10S, C1 is 100nF instead of the required >=10µF for the LM1117-5.0 output, and two ATtiny microcontrollers are connected in parallel on all pins, which would cause contention if both are populated."
}

